----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The X11 colour-name table, so that `background = cornflower blue` in a config
file means what it means everywhere else. Data, not code, and it is compiled
into `Illogical.app` alone -- neither `illogicald` nor the CLI reads a config
file, so neither carries it.

The file is byte for byte the copy libghostty embeds. It carries no header of
its own -- every line is a colour -- so its terms are not reproducible from
this tree; ghostty states them beside its copy, in
`src/terminal/x11_color.zig`:

    This is the rgb.txt file from the X11 project. This was last sourced
    from this location: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/app/rgb
    This data is licensed under the MIT/X11 license while this Zig file is
    licensed under the same license as Ghostty.

The MIT/X11 text is the one reproduced under `ghostty` at the top of this
file, with the X.Org Foundation and its contributors in place of the copyright
holders named there. The upstream repository above carries the authoritative
copy.
